config COUNTER_MCP79XX
	bool "Microchip MCP79xx RTC driver (out-of-tree)"
	default y
	depends on DT_HAS_MICROCHIP_MCP79XX_ENABLED
	depends on I2C
	depends on RTC
	help
	  Out-of-tree MCP79xx driver registering the Zephyr RTC API only
	  (compatible "microchip,mcp79xx"). Fixes year encoding (years since
	  2000 → tm_year offset 100) vs upstream counter driver bugs.

	  Requires CONFIG_RTC=y (do not select RTC here — that creates
	  circular select deps with other RTC drivers such as DS1307).

	  Features:
	  - RTC API: set/get time, optional alarms + calibration
	  - 24-hour format (avoids errata #1 12h date-increment issue)
	  - Calibration: OSCTRIM ±127 (±129 ppm physical); Zephyr polarity
	  - MFP GPIO for alarm IRQ (IF clear only until Track B)

	  Supported register map: MCP7940M/N and related MCP79xx parts.
	  This product targets MCP7940N (VBAT switchover). Binding "variant"
	  is informational today — not used for feature gating.
